  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSample Ballots - Elections - Mahaska County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Mahaska County\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Mahaska County Elections\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPoll Workers\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections Sample Ballots\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nFilter by Year\n \n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \nView All\n \n \nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPoll Workers\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n2026 Elections \n\n 2026 General Election\n \n\n November 3, 2026\n\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n29 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n \n\n June 2, 2026\n\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n \n4 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2025 Elections \n\n City/School Election\n \n\n November 4, 2025\n\n City/School Election \n \n\n Beginning in 2019, School and City Elections will be combined and held in November of odd-numbered years. A City election is used to elect the Mayor and Council Members and any other elected city officials. In Mahaska County, Oskaloosa has a provision that could cause a run-off election to take place in December. That happens when a candidate does not receive enough votes to be declared the winner. A School Election is an election to select School Board members for school districts within Mahaska County. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n Oskaloosa City Council Special Election\n \n\n August 5, 2025\n\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2024 Elections \n\n 2024 General Election\n \n\n November 5, 2024\n\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n30 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n 2024 Primary Election\n \n\n June 4, 2024\n\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n \n3 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2023 Elections \n\n 2023 City School Election\n \n\n November 7, 2023\n\n City/School Election \n \n\n Beginning in 2019, School and City Elections will be combined and held in November of odd-numbered years. A City election is used to elect the Mayor and Council Members and any other elected city officials. In Mahaska County, Oskaloosa has a provision that could cause a run-off election to take place in December. That happens when a candidate does not receive enough votes to be declared the winner. A School Election is an election to select School Board members for school districts within Mahaska County. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2022 Elections \n\n 2022 General Election\n \n\n November 8, 2022\n\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n34 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n 2022 City of Eddyville Special Election\n \n\n September 13, 2022\n\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n 2022 Primary Election\n \n\n June 7, 2022\n\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2021 Elections \n\n 2021 City/School Election\n \n\n November 2, 2021\n\n City/School Election \n \n\n Beginning in 2019, School and City Elections will be combined and held in November of odd-numbered years. A City election is used to elect the Mayor and Council Members and any other elected city officials. In Mahaska County, Oskaloosa has a provision that could cause a run-off election to take place in December. That happens when a candidate does not receive enough votes to be declared the winner. A School Election is an election to select School Board members for school districts within Mahaska County. \n \n2 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2020 Elections \n\n General Election\n \n\n November 3, 2020\n\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n28 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n Primary Election\n \n\n June 2, 2020\n\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n\n2019 Elections \n\n City/School Election\n \n\n November 5, 2019\n\n City/School Election \n \n\n Beginning in 2019, School and City Elections will be combined and held in November of odd-numbered years. A City election is used to elect the Mayor and Council Members and any other elected city officials. In Mahaska County, Oskaloosa has a provision that could cause a run-off election to take place in December. That happens when a candidate does not receive enough votes to be declared the winner. A School Election is an election to select School Board members for school districts within Mahaska County. \n \n1 Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Mahaska County Auditor\n\n Mahaska County Courthouse, 1st Floor\n\n 106 South 1st Street\n\n Oskaloosa, Iowa 52577\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00AM to 4:30PM\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (641) 673-7148\n\n Fax: (641) 673-2597\n\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Mahaska County Elections\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
}
